    "highlights": "Syntax highlighting and specific brand colors are applied to typography in product demos (e.g., #DB90A5, #FFEA00 for code, and #DD55E7 for feature callouts), functioning as specialized inline highlighting techniques.",
    "insights": [
      "Highly utilitarian typography scaling down to extreme micro sizes (6px-10px) to realistically render complex UI mockups (like Slack, Code Editor, and Apple Notes within the hero section).",
      "The system mixes a primary brand sans-serif (Inter) with native system fonts (-apple-system, ui-monospace) for rendering native-looking UI components within the product demonstrations.",
      "Typography is optimized for dense data and application interfaces, prioritizing legibility at extremely small sizes with precise line-height control and tracking (e.g., -0.025em for headings)."
